# Input for .github/ci/requirements-docs-guards.txt - the HASHED install set
# of docs-guards.yml (the md-reading guards). Deliberately small: it does NOT
# include the root requirements.in. It installs the runtime packages the
# selected modules are MEASURED to execute (below) and nothing else; every
# other package requirements.in pins is declared NOT installed, with a reason,
# on a `# docs-guards-not-installed: <name> - <reason>` line.
# tests/test_ci_docs_guard_coverage.py fails on a requirements.in package that
# is neither installed by the .txt nor declared here, so a new runtime
# dependency is classified on purpose, never inherited by accident.
#
# CI installs the generated .txt with `pip install --require-hashes`. Never
# hand-edit the .txt: change this file and regenerate, from the repo root,
# with:
#
#   uv pip compile .github/ci/requirements-docs-guards.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --output-file .github/ci/requirements-docs-guards.txt
#
# --python-version / --python-platform name the RUNNER (ubuntu-latest,
# setup-python 3.12), so the output is the same on any host. Dependabot's
# `pip` entry for /.github/ci keeps the pins and hashes current.

# pydantic follows the runtime pin rather than floating: one source of truth
# for a version, not two. The constraint is the root requirements.in (the
# top-level pins), not the hashed requirements.txt generated from it.
-c ../../requirements.in

pytest
pytest-asyncio
pytest-timeout
# Test-only: the workflow-shape assertions in tests/test_ci_docs_guard_coverage.py.
# Without it they degrade to skips, and a skipped test is a green tick.
pyyaml
pydantic

# Runtime packages the selection EXECUTES. MEASURED 2026-10-31, docs-guards run
# 41216101159 (8 failed): the s144 selector widening (RM-1107, RM-1145..RM-1147)
# picks modules whose NON-md tests load them. Versions follow requirements.in
# through the -c line above.
#   json5       - tools/daemon_slayer_extract.py, loaded by
#                 agents/daemon_slayer/tests/test_artifact_patch_marker_guard.py
#                 and tests/test_tracked_json_producers_emit_lf_bytes.py
#   anthropic   - tft/tft_coach_engine.py, tests/test_tft_meta_provenance_rm846.py
#   portalocker - core/decision_detector.py, imported by the dashboard POST
#                 dispatch inside tests/test_dead_endpoint_cleanup_item186.py's
#                 in-process server (its absence read as RemoteDisconnected)
json5
anthropic
portalocker

# Pinned in requirements.in, NOT installed here (machine-read lines; the reason
# is required). Move a name up into the list above, and drop its line here,
# when a selected module is measured executing it.
# docs-guards-not-installed: certifi - no selected module executes it (41216101159), and anthropic 1.11.0 does not pull it in (httpx2 + truststore)
# docs-guards-not-installed: opencv-python - imaging stack (a ~60 MB wheel plus numpy); no selected module executes cv2 (41216101159)
# docs-guards-not-installed: Pillow - imaging stack; no selected module executes PIL (41216101159)
# docs-guards-not-installed: psutil - no selected module executes it (41216101159); left out so the job stays as small as its selection needs
# docs-guards-not-installed: websockets - no selected module executes it (41216101159); left out so the job stays as small as its selection needs
